Vrinda Store (31,047 order lines, ₹2.12 crore gross sales)

What the data shows


Revenue leakage: ₹1.97 crore of the gross sales were delivered (93.1%). About ₹14.7 lakh (6.9%) was lost to returns, cancellations and refunds. Returns are the biggest part at ₹7.2 lakh. 
The rate is similar on every channel (7–8%), so this is a product or fulfilment issue, not a channel issue.

Women drive volume, men spend more per order. Women are 64% of sales and 69% of order lines, but men’s average order is ₹802 against ₹629 for women (about 27% higher).

Age 30–49 is the core segment, with 50% of revenue. Women aged 30–49 alone bring in about 32%. Under-30s are 30% and 50+ are 20%.

Sales are concentrated by state. Maharashtra leads (₹29.9 lakh), then Karnataka, Uttar Pradesh, Telangana and Tamil Nadu. These five are 53% of sales. Bengaluru is the top city.

Three channels carry the business. Amazon, Myntra and Flipkart together are 80% of sales, with Amazon alone at 35%. Average order value is about ₹682 on every channel, so channel mix drives revenue, not pricing.

Sets are the star category. They bring in 50% of revenue from 40% of orders, at ₹848 per order. Kurtas are 34% of orders but only 23% of revenue (₹475 per order), so upselling kurta buyers to sets is the 
clearest opportunity. Bottoms are almost nothing (₹0.28 lakh).

Size demand is wider than expected. M and L lead, but about 40% of units are XL or larger. Stock planning should reflect that.
